<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Hyderabad (1843)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1843</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Dubba</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad-sindh">Hyderabad</a>, also called the Battle of Dubba, was fought on 24 March 1843 near Hyderabad in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a>. A British force under Charles Napier defeated the army of the Talpur ruler Mir Sher Muhammad of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirpur-khas">Mirpur Khas</a>. Following the earlier victory at Miani, it completed the British conquest of Sindh, which was annexed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mumbai">Bombay</a> Presidency.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-hyderabad-1843.jpg" alt="Battle of Hyderabad (1843)" width="320" height="168" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Jones · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Battle_of_Hyderabad,_24_March_1843.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
